--- run under cc_backend_fast_math=true ---
--- leg 1: the gate -- key off keeps the composed form ---
composed: no scan in the routine: true
composed: the routine writes seq^2-sized intermediates: true
composed: every output is finite: true
--- leg 2: causal attention, head width under the recompute cap ---
rewritten: exactly one scan, the attention's online normalizer: true
the pass changes the raw lowering: true
the pass is idempotent on its own output: true
rewritten: no seq^2-sized node is written at all: true
rewritten output matches the composed output within 1e-5 relative: true
--- leg 3: head width above the recompute cap -- the cap owns the scores ---
seq^2 buffers: composed 2, rewritten 1
rewritten: the scores are the one seq^2 buffer left (the probabilities are gone): true
rewritten output matches the composed output within 1e-5 relative: true
a cap admitting the head width recomputes the scores: no seq^2 buffer at all: true
recomputed scores give the same output within 1e-5 relative: true
--- leg 4: masked key prefixes -- the recurrence survives -inf scores ---
rewritten: every output is finite: true
rewritten output matches the composed output within 1e-5 relative: true
--- leg 5: two stacked blocks -- one scan each ---
rewritten: two scans: true
rewritten: no seq^2-sized node is written: true
rewritten output matches the composed output within 1e-5 relative: true
--- leg 6: training -- parameter gradients agree with the composed forward ---
the loss agrees within 1e-5 relative: true
parameters with gradients: 4
the same parameters carry gradients in both runs: true
w_q_attn0.grad agrees within 1e-4 relative: true
w_q_attn0.grad is not identically zero: true
w_k_attn0.grad agrees within 1e-4 relative: true
w_k_attn0.grad is not identically zero: true
w_v_attn0.grad agrees within 1e-4 relative: true
w_v_attn0.grad is not identically zero: true
w_o_attn0.grad agrees within 1e-4 relative: true
w_o_attn0.grad is not identically zero: true
--- leg 7: the recognizer declines what it cannot prove, on hand-built lowerings ---
the composed order is rewritten into one scan: true
the subtraction ahead of the max is declined: true
the exponential after the sum is declined: true
a read of the normalizer between its zeroing and the max is declined: true
a read of the normalizer between the max and the sum is declined: true
the zeroing ahead of the max with nothing reading the normalizer in between is accepted: true
staged code inside the span the rewrite reorders is declined: true
a Tile_mma inside the span is opaque even when its scalar fallback is empty: true
staged code outside that span is no objection: true
staged code reachable only through a guard's condition inside the span is declined too: true
a scope body inside the span is beyond the write census and declines the rewrite: true
a whole-node zeroing of a normalizer wider than the reduction's cells is declined: true
the same reduction with a cell-wise zeroing is accepted: the scan writes what the fill did: true
composed: a NaN score ahead of a masked one poisons the normalizer: true
rewritten: the all-masked step after the NaN keeps the poison: true
a genuinely all-masked prefix leaves both normalizers finite and equal within 1e-6 relative: true
an f16 chain: the f32-carried normalizer agrees with the per-step-rounded one within 2e-3: true
a row of scores at the format's lowest finite value is a finite maximum in both forms, with the row length as normalizer: true
a fully masked row leaves the composed normalizer NaN: true
and the rewritten normalizer stores that NaN too, though its carried state stayed zero: true
the value reduction is hoisted through a ten-nest elementwise chain from the probabilities: true
a reduction whose target cell is [t + j] is not hoisted: distinct pairs share a cell: true
a dead moved loop is not hoisted: the original nest never reads the probability: true
an integer normalizer node is declined: its own reduction truncated after every step: true
an auxiliary subtraction and exponential ahead of the normalizer's own do not hide it: true
a max node narrower than the scores is declined: the composed max rounds where the state does not: true
a max node of the scores' range but fewer digits (bf16 under f32) is declined too: true
an exponential node narrower than the scores is declined: small terms round to zero there: true
a normalizer wider than the chain (f64 under f32) is declined: it would sum unrounded terms: true
scores narrower than the chain (f16 under f32) are declined as well: one precision throughout: true
a chain at one precision is accepted at f16: true
an f64 chain carries both states at double: true
an f16 chain carries both states at single: widened, never per-step at the storage width: true
--- leg 8: a NaN mask fill poisons the rewritten rows exactly where it poisons the composed ---
the composed output is NaN in every row: every row has a NaN-filled position: true
the rewritten output is NaN exactly where the composed output is: true
--- leg 8b: sibling lowerings of one rewritten program hit the analysis cache ---
re-lowering the rewritten forward is an analysis-cache hit, not a miss: true
